# EF Core 10 Breaking Changes for Your Code

## 1. `SetProperty` value argument must be a lambda expression

In EF Core 10, the manually-constructed expression tree for `SetProperty` requires the **value** argument to be an `Expression<Func<TSource, TProperty>>` lambda, not a bare `Expression.Constant`.

**Fix:**

```csharp
var blogParameter = Expression.Parameter(typeof(Blog), "b");
var valueParam = Expression.Parameter(typeof(Blog), "b2");

setters = Expression.Lambda<Func<SetPropertyCalls<Blog>, SetPropertyCalls<Blog>>>(
    Expression.Call(
        instance: setters.Body,
        methodName: nameof(SetPropertyCalls<Blog>.SetProperty),
        typeArguments: new[] { typeof(string) },
        arguments: new Expression[]
        {
            Expression.Lambda<Func<Blog, string>>(
                Expression.Property(blogParameter, nameof(Blog.Name)), blogParameter),
            // Wrap constant in a lambda:
            Expression.Lambda<Func<Blog, string>>(
                Expression.Constant("foo"), valueParam)
        }),
    setters.Parameters);
```

---

## 2. Complex properties with the same CLR type require explicit configuration

EF Core 10 now validates that complex properties sharing a CLR type have **distinct type names** to avoid ambiguous column mappings. Configure with `ComplexTypePropertyBuilder.HasTypeName`:

**Fix:**

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, a => a.HasTypeName("ShippingAddress"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, a => a.HasTypeName("BillingAddress"));
});

// For nested complex types, apply at each level:
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, pb =>
    {
        pb.ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress, a => a.HasTypeName("PaymentBillingAddress"));
    });
});
```

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` gains a `CommandSource` parameter

EF Core 10 added a `CommandSource` parameter to the diagnostics interface methods to indicate what triggered the command.

**Fix:**

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        CommandSource commandSource)   // <-- new parameter
    { /* logging */ }
}
```

---

## Summary

| Issue | Root cause | One-line fix |
|-------|-----------|--------------|
| `ExecuteUpdateAsync` throws at runtime | Value arg must be a lambda expression tree | Wrap `Expression.Constant(...)` in `Expression.Lambda(...)` |
| Complex type model validation fails | Same CLR type used for multiple complex properties | Add `HasTypeName(...)` to each complex property |
| Build error on diagnostics logger | New `CommandSource` parameter added to interface | Add the parameter to your implementation |
